Root cause:
The bug was caused by the allocation of a large cpumask on the stack in the function `hv_send_ipi_mask_allbutself`, which could consume significant stack space (up to 1 kilobyte) if the kernel was configured for a large number of CPUs (e.g., 8192). This practice is not advisable as it risks stack overflow and can lead to undefined behavior. The patch removes this on-stack allocation by modifying the function to exclude the current CPU directly in the existing helper functions, thus improving memory usage and stability.
